# Files that decide what every other change is allowed to do. GitHub requests a
# review from the owner listed here whenever a pull request touches one of them.
#
# It requests; it does not require. The branch ruleset in
# `.github/rulesets/main.json` sets `require_code_owner_review` to false, and its
# `reviewPolicy` says why: a sole maintainer cannot approve their own pull
# request, so requiring one would block every merge. Turn it on the day a second
# reviewer exists — these entries are what it will then enforce.
#
# A downstream product replaces the handle: see `docs/repository-host.md`.

